\f0\fs36 \cf0 PLEASE READ THESE INSTRUCTIONS FIRST.\
  \
This is a test for the blind spot of your left eye.  During the test, keep your right eye closed and look steadily at the 'X' from a distance of about 11 inches. When you first touch the screen, a  test spot will be presented within your blindspot, to the left of the 'X'.  Each touch on the screen (up to a total of eight times) will move the spot away from the blindspot center until you can see it. (Don't worry--it won't move on its own.) When you THINK you see the spot (don't be fussy), touch the \'91X\'92 to record the position.  After you touch the \'91X\'92, a new test spot will start within the blindspot, and will move outward in a new direction until you see it again.  Touch the \'91X\'92 again when you see this one.  Six other directions will be tested, for a total of eight:  you will see a little note above 'Start Test' to let you know how many of the eight directions you have completed.  It is OK to look away from the 'X' to check your progress, provided you return your attention to the 'X' while the test spots are being shown.  After all directions have been tested, you may touch the \'91Result\'92 button to see the outline of your blindspot.  Congratulations!  You have just performed your first visual field test.  With your test result shown on the screen, look again at the 'X' (still with your left eye alone) and the spots will disappear!   \
\
TO TEST THE RIGHT EYE, TURN iPAD UPSIDE DOWN.\
\
OTHER MEASUREMENT SUGGESTIONS:  put the iPad down on a flat surface and use a vertical pad of 8.5 x 11 inch paper placed just to the right of the 'X' (or to the left, if testing right eye) to maintain your 11 inch distance from the screen.  It will also block your non-tested eye from seeing the test spot, so you don't have to hold it closed. \
\
\ul When you have finished the test\ulnone , you may use the Camera icon at the top of the ipad screen to save your rest result.\
 \
Now go ahead and touch 'Move to Test' at the bottom of the page}